---
import MarketingLayout from '../layouts/MarketingLayout.astro';
import Section from '../components/Section.astro';
import Button from '../components/Button.astro';
import { process, comparison, fit, whoItsFor } from '../data/home';
import { Check, X, Minus } from '@lucide/astro';
---
<MarketingLayout
  title="How a problem becomes software"
  description="Supply-chain operations understood before a line of code — then AI orchestration to ship fast. Working software that's yours to own, not a deck."
>
  {/* ── Intro ───────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────
      D113 CARRIED OFF THE HOME PAGE, 2026-09-13. This page was the purest
      instance of the complaint D113 was raised on: SIX bands, every single one
      at max-w-4xl, every single one on the same vertical rhythm, with canvas
      and surface alternating underneath on a fixed beat. Nothing but the ground
      ever moved, and the ground moved on a metronome.

      It now walks feature, popout, content, feature, content, popout for the
      column and canvas, deep, surface, canvas, deep, canvas for the ground,
      with the rhythm moving under both. No two neighbors share more than one
      heavy signal and the palette does none of the work — a hue is the lightest
      signal on a page, which is the argument src/components/kit/industrial.js
      makes under WHY THREE AND NOT SEVEN.

      THE TWO WEIGH-UPS GET DIFFERENT GROUNDS, AND THAT IS THE POINT RATHER THAN
      DECORATION. The difference band and the fit band are both two panels side
      by side asking a reader to weigh one column against another, built from
      nearly the same markup, with only a band of cards between them. Rendered
      on one ground at one width they would read as the same argument made
      twice, which is the defect one level down from where D113 found it — the
      same reading /services/ wrote down over its five identical doors. */}
  <Section width="feature" class="border-b border-line">
    <Fragment slot="backdrop">
      <div class="bg-grid bg-grid-fade pointer-events-none absolute inset-0 -z-10 opacity-60"></div>
    </Fragment>
      <p class="mono-label">Approach</p>
      <h1 class="statement mt-3 max-w-3xl">
        Domain mastery, directing AI, into working software.
      </h1>
      <p class="mt-5 max-w-2xl text-lg leading-relaxed text-ink-muted">
        The hard part isn’t the AI — it’s knowing exactly <span class="aiq-accent">what to build</span>, and building it so you
        actually own it. This is how I do it, and who it’s for.
      </p>
      <p class="mt-6 text-sm text-ink-muted">
        New here?{' '}
        <a href="/bio/" class="link-sweep">
          Start with who I am →
        </a>
      </p>
  </Section>

  {/* ── The method ──────────────────────────────────────────────────────────
      THE DEEP GROUND IS HERE FOR THE LIST RATHER THAN FOR THE ARGUMENT, which
      is the one place on this page the ground is chosen by what sits on it. The
      steps are `bg-surface` rows separated by hairlines; on the surface band
      they would have been surface on surface, and the rows that are meant to
      read as raised would have read as a flat block with lines drawn in it. On
      surface-2 they sit a step above their ground and the separators do the job
      they were drawn for.

      The reading column goes with it. A numbered method is read top to bottom
      one step at a time, and the widest measure on the page is the last thing
      it wants. The numerals above the labels are gone from this page — PICKUP.md
      scores a decorative "/ 01" as a generated-design signal, and on a page
      where four of them numbered sections a reader can arrive at in any order,
      they were numbering something that is not a sequence. */}
  <Section tone="deep" width="popout">
    <p class="mono-label">The method</p>
    <h2 class="mt-3 font-display text-3xl font-semibold tracking-[-0.03em] text-ink sm:text-4xl">
      How a problem becomes a tool.
    </h2>

    <ol class="mt-10 flex flex-col gap-px overflow-hidden rounded-xl border border-line bg-line">
      {process.map((step) => (
        <li class="flex flex-col gap-4 bg-surface p-6 sm:flex-row sm:gap-6 sm:p-8">
          <span class="process-node shrink-0">{step.n}</span>
          <div>
            <h3 class="font-display text-xl font-semibold text-ink">{step.title}</h3>
            <p class="mt-2 leading-relaxed text-ink-muted">{step.body}</p>
          </div>
        </li>
      ))}
    </ol>
  </Section>

  {/* ── Working software vs. slideware ──────────────────────────────────────
      The first of the two weigh-ups, and it takes the surface ground, the
      widest rhythm on the page and a column wide enough that neither side of
      the comparison is read at a different measure from the other. This is the
      band the page is actually arguing in, so it is the band that gets the air.

      `surface` AND NOT `instrument`: the right-hand panel carries
      border-accent/40, a literal sized for a light ground that no band can
      remap — the same reading src/pages/work/index.astro and /websites/ wrote
      down when each declined the dark chassis for a panel of its own. */}
  <Section tone="surface" width="content" density="tall">
      <p class="mono-label">The difference</p>
      <h2 class="mt-3 font-display text-3xl font-semibold tracking-[-0.03em] text-ink sm:text-4xl">
        It ends at a tool people use — not a slide.
      </h2>

      <div class="mt-10 grid gap-4 md:grid-cols-2">
        <div class="panel lift spotlight p-7">
          <p class="mono-label">{comparison.left.title}</p>
          <ul class="mt-5 flex flex-col gap-3">
            {comparison.left.items.map((item) => (
              <li class="flex items-start gap-3 text-ink-muted">
                <X size={18} class="mt-0.5 shrink-0 text-down" aria-hidden="true" />
                <span>{item}</span>
              </li>
            ))}
          </ul>
        </div>
        <div class="panel lift spotlight border-accent/40 p-7">
          <p class="mono-label text-cyan-deep">{comparison.right.title}</p>
          <ul class="mt-5 flex flex-col gap-3">
            {comparison.right.items.map((item) => (
              <li class="flex items-start gap-3 text-ink">
                <Check size={18} class="mt-0.5 shrink-0 text-up" aria-hidden="true" />
                <span>{item}</span>
              </li>
            ))}
          </ul>
        </div>
      </div>
  </Section>

  {/* ── Who I build for ─────────────────────────────────────────────────────
      Back to the page's own ground, out to the widest column, and tight under
      the tallest band on the page. Four cards at max-w-4xl were being asked to
      hold a persona each in a quarter of 56rem; the feature measure is what
      lets the fourth column carry a sentence rather than a stack of single
      words, and it is the only band here with four things in a row. */}
  <Section width="feature" density="tight">
    <p class="mono-label">Who I help</p>
    <h2 class="mt-3 font-display text-3xl font-semibold tracking-[-0.03em] text-ink sm:text-4xl">
      Who I build for — and the problem they’re carrying.
    </h2>

    <div class="mt-10 grid gap-4 sm:grid-cols-2 lg:grid-cols-4">
      {whoItsFor.map((p) => (
        <div class="panel lift spotlight flex flex-col gap-3 p-6">
          <h3 class="font-display text-lg font-semibold text-ink">{p.title}</h3>
          <p class="text-sm leading-relaxed text-ink-muted">{p.body}</p>
        </div>
      ))}
    </div>
  </Section>

  {/* ── Fit / not a fit ─────────────────────────────────────────────────────
      The second weigh-up, and it is on the deep ground for the reason given at
      the top of this file: it is built from nearly the same markup as the
      difference band and asks the reader to do the same thing with it. A
      different ground and a column a step narrower are what stop the two
      reading as one argument made twice. This one is the colder of the pair —
      it is the band that talks a reader out of the work — so it sits lower than
      the band that argues for it, and it does not get the extra air. */}
  <Section tone="deep" width="content">
      <p class="mono-label">Fit</p>
      <h2 class="mt-3 font-display text-3xl font-semibold tracking-[-0.03em] text-ink sm:text-4xl">
        A fit — and a not-a-fit.
      </h2>

      <div class="mt-10 grid gap-4 md:grid-cols-2">
        <div class="panel lift spotlight p-7">
          <p class="mono-label text-up">A fit when</p>
          <ul class="mt-5 flex flex-col gap-3">
            {fit.fit.map((item) => (
              <li class="flex items-start gap-3 text-ink">
                <Check size={18} class="mt-0.5 shrink-0 text-up" aria-hidden="true" />
                <span>{item}</span>
              </li>
            ))}
          </ul>
        </div>
        <div class="panel lift spotlight p-7">
          <p class="mono-label text-down">Not a fit if</p>
          <ul class="mt-5 flex flex-col gap-3">
            {fit.notFit.map((item) => (
              <li class="flex items-start gap-3 text-ink-muted">
                <Minus size={18} class="mt-0.5 shrink-0 text-down" aria-hidden="true" />
                <span>{item}</span>
              </li>
            ))}
          </ul>
        </div>
      </div>
  </Section>

  {/* ── CTA ─────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────
      The narrowest column and the shortest rhythm on the page, back on canvas.
      A centered ask is two lines and two buttons; giving it the same measure as
      the argument above made the page end on an empty band rather than on a
      question. */}
  <Section width="popout" density="tight" class="text-center">
    <h2 class="font-display text-2xl font-semibold tracking-[-0.03em] text-ink sm:text-3xl">
      Have a problem that fits?
    </h2>
    <div class="mt-7 flex flex-wrap items-center justify-center gap-3">
      <Button href="/contact/" variant="primary">Start a project</Button>
      <Button href="/work/" variant="secondary">See the live tools</Button>
    </div>
  </Section>
</MarketingLayout>
